# Every discoverable area of Teldrassil, Darkshore, Ashenvale, Stonetalon
# Mountains, The Barrens, Durotar, Mulgore, Thousand Needles (110 map overlays),
# for both factions. Each `explore` point is the centre of the area's map
# overlay hit rect in the Forever client's tables (WorldMapOverlay,
# UiMapXMapArt, UiMap, AreaTable via wago.tools, build 1.60.1.70338), in the
# map's live frame (written `live` where Forever moved the map or added it, else
# the Era frame it equals); area levels are AreaTable.ExplorationLevel; flight
# masters come from data/forever/travel.json. Zone order and travel lines are
# tools/lib/exploration/spec.js; inside a zone the areas are a shortest tour
# from where you arrive towards the next zone.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Alliance

step Teldrassil (1/2)
  only Alliance
  zone Teldrassil
  tip Discovering an area gives experience scaled to its level, so this runs alongside leveling. Alliance starts on Teldrassil; humans, dwarves and gnomes arrive by boat at Auberdine and can begin at the Darkshore step. 11 areas to discover here, levels 5-11.
  note "Exploring the entire world map on one character is a Forever Legacy Challenge (1 account-wide Legacy Point)."
  note "Shadowglen opens onto Teldrassil; Dolanaar is south along the road. Rut'theran Village, at the foot of the tree, is reached through the portal in Darnassus."
  note "Flight path here: Rut'theran Village (Vesprystus)."
  explore 59.6,40 "Shadowglen"
  explore 65.6,57.6 "Starbreeze Village"
  explore 57.6,71.1 "Lake Al'Ameth"
  explore 55.6,90.9 "Rut'theran Village"
  explore 43.9,74.9 "Gnarlpine Hold"
  explore 40.4,63.6 "Pools of Arlithrien"

